### Layer boundaries

The architecture contract is fixed in [`CLAUDE.md`](../CLAUDE.md). The rules that
matter for review:

| Rule | Why |
|---|---|
| **No module outside `backend/config.py` calls `os.getenv`** | One source of truth for configuration; no hidden environment coupling |
| **No module in `backend/` touches a datastore directly** | All access goes through `db.sqlite.models` or `db.vectordb.vector_store`, which is what makes the pgvector migration a one-file change |
| **Handoffs between graph nodes are validated Pydantic objects** | A node never passes free text to another node; a malformed model response becomes a schema default, not corrupted downstream state |
| **All ticketing systems are reached through `TicketSource`** | Vendor coupling confined to one file per vendor |
| **Every write tool re-checks authorisation itself** | The route that set a status is never trusted as sufficient evidence of approval |

