## 7. Data architecture

### 7.1 Relational store — SQLite (`db/sqlite/data/app.db`)

| Table | Purpose | Key columns |
|---|---|---|
| `users` | Identity and clearance | `username`, `password_hash` (Werkzeug salted), `role`, `clearances` (JSON), `email` |
| `tickets` | The operational governance record | `external_id` + `source` (unique together), `title`, `body_masked`, `reporter`, `assignee`, `application`, `environment`, `category`, `subcategory`, `severity`, `priority_score`, `assigned_team`, `status`, `confidence`, `needs_human`, `overridden_by`, `override_reason`, `true_category`/`true_severity`/`true_team`, `held_out`, `sync_attempts`, `last_error`, `sla_warning_sent_at` |
| `triage_runs` | One row per agent execution | `ticket_id`, `decision_json`, `model`, `tier`, `tokens`, `cost_usd`, `latency_ms`, `trace_id`, `guardrails_fired` |
| `documents` | KB governance record | `filename`, `modality`, `allowed_roles`, `sensitivity`, `chunk_count`, `attributes` (doc_type/team/service) |
| `chat_sessions` / `chat_messages` | Conversation state | `summary`; per-message `citations`, `latency_ms`, tokens, `groundedness`, `blocked_reason` |
| `audit_log` | Append-only hash chain | `action`, `resource`, `details`, `prev_hash`, `entry_hash` |
| `feedback` | Human correction signal | `message_id`, `rating` (±1), `comment`, `corrected_answer`, `reviewed` |
| `eval_results` | Persisted eval runs | `groundedness`, `context_precision`, `context_recall`, `hallucination` |
| `sync_state` | Ingestion watermark | `source` (PK), `watermark` |

**Ticket status lifecycle:**

```
new → triaged → awaiting_approval → routed → synced
                        ↘ failed (dead letter, still visible to a human)
```

**Schema evolution.** `Base.metadata.create_all()` only creates missing tables; it
never alters an existing one. `_migrate_sqlite_columns()` runs on every boot and
adds missing columns additively, so a live database never needs a manual wipe
because the schema grew.

### 7.2 Vector store — Chroma (`db/vectordb/data/chroma/`)

| Property | Value |
|---|---|
| Collection | `knowledge_base` |
| Distance | Cosine (`hnsw:space: cosine`); score = `1.0 − distance` |
| Vector dimension | 3072 (`text-embedding-3-large`) |
| Chunk size / overlap | 900 / 150 characters |
| Chunk metadata | `doc_id`, `filename`, `doc_type`, `team`, `service`, `severity`, `category`, `environment`, `resolved`, `modality`, `sensitivity`, `allowed_roles`, `acl_<role>` booleans, `page` |

Chunking uses a separator order tuned to ticket and runbook structure —
`## Symptom`, `## Diagnosis`, `## Fix`, `Steps to reproduce`, `Environment`, `Logs`
— so a chunk boundary lands between sections rather than mid-procedure. PDF pages
carry `[[PAGE:n]]` markers so a citation can name a page.

> A file named `chroma.sqlite3` inside the Chroma directory is **Chroma's own
> internal storage**, not a third database. Never edit it directly.

### 7.3 Corpora

| Corpus | `doc_type` | Volume | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| Historical tickets | `ticket_history` | 400 indexed | The precedent library |
| Held-out tickets | — | 100 | Gold labels only, **never embedded** — the exam the system cannot study for |
| Runbooks | `runbook` | 24 | One per team/service pair |
| Service catalogue | `service_catalog` | 1 | Service → owning team; the routing ground truth |
| SLA policy | `sla_policy` | 1 | Priority → response/resolution minutes |
| Escalation matrix | `escalation_matrix` | 1 | `restricted` sensitivity |

**All data is synthetic.** No real customer data, no real incident records, no
production identifiers. The corpus is generated with deliberate realism — typos,
half-pasted stack traces, duplicate reports of one outage, and planted secrets that
exercise the redaction path — because a triage system tested only on clean input is
not tested.

### 7.4 Data lifecycle and retention

| Data | Retention | Deletion path |
|---|---|---|
| Ticket content | Persisted masked; raw text never stored | `DELETE /api/documents/<id>` removes SQLite row and Chroma chunks together |
| PII | Masked at ingest before storage or embedding | Irreversible for secrets; reversible tokens for structured identifiers |
| Chat history | Per session, user-deletable | `DELETE /api/sessions/<id>`, `DELETE /api/chatbot/history` |
| Audit log | Append-only, never deleted by design | Full-store reset only |
| Uploads | `db/vectordb/data/uploads/` | Removed with the document |

**Prototype-to-enterprise gap:** no automated retention timer, no legal-hold
support, and no per-tenant encryption at rest. All three are storage-layer concerns
that move with the pgvector/Postgres migration.

