## 9. Retrieval architecture (RAG)

### 9.1 Ingestion pipeline

```
file / paste / ticket
  → extract (PyMuPDF; vision model for pages with < 120 chars of text)
  → anonymize (regex → secret wipe → optional LLM pass)
  → chunk (900 / 150, section-aware, page markers)
  → embed (text-embedding-3-large, batch 32)
  → Chroma upsert with governance metadata
  → SQLite `documents` / `tickets` mirror
```

Tickets skip the LLM anonymisation pass at index time because
`triage_normalize` has already masked them — re-running it would double latency
and tokens for no benefit.

### 9.2 Query pipeline

| Stage | Parameter | Value |
|---|---|---|
| Query rewrite | conversation summary + history | chat surface only |
| Query decompose | max sub-queries | 3 |
| Dense candidates | `RETRIEVE_TOP_K` | 20 |
| Lexical | BM25Okapi, hits with score > 0 | — |
| Fusion | Reciprocal Rank Fusion, `RRF_K` | 60 |
| Rerank | cross-encoder `ms-marco-MiniLM-L-6-v2` | available, **off by default** |
| Final context | `FINAL_TOP_K` (chat) / `TRIAGE_ENRICH_TOP_K` (triage) | 6 / 8 |
| ACL | Chroma `where` clause | applied **inside** the query |
| Metadata filters | `doc_type`, `team`, `service`, `environment`, `category`, `severity`, `resolved` | merged into `where` |

**No minimum similarity threshold** is applied at the vector layer — relevance is
enforced by the CRAG `grade` node instead, which can read the chunks in context
rather than trusting a distance number. A score cut-off would silently drop a
correct-but-differently-worded precedent.

**ACL is a query clause, never a post-filter.** A post-filter degrades top-k
silently for restricted users: ask for 6, retrieve 6, discard 4, show 2. Filtering
inside the query means a restricted user gets 6 chunks they are entitled to see,
and unauthorised text never enters the prompt at all. A defence-in-depth
`can_read()` check runs on the returned set as well.

### 9.3 Why the priority rulebook is injected, not retrieved

`docs/PRIORITY_RULEBOOK.md` is loaded whole into the prompt. Retrieval returns
*part* of a document; two identical tickets scored against different fragments of
the same rubric would be silently non-deterministic. A rubric is applied whole or
it is not a rubric.

