## 10. Model strategy

### 10.1 Tier assignment and rationale

| Tier | Model | Nodes | Why |
|---|---|---|---|
| **deep** | `genailab-maas-gpt-5.1` | `assess`, `reflect` | Highest blast radius. A wrong `Highest` pages an on-call at 3am; a missed `Highest` breaches a contractual SLA. Reflection must be able to genuinely find its own errors, which a weaker model cannot. |
| **standard** | `azure/genailab-maas-gpt-4.1` | `classify`, `route`, chat generation, suggested action | Constrained decisions over supplied evidence with an enum output space. Strong general capability is sufficient; deep-tier cost is not justified. |
| **fast** | `azure/genailab-maas-gpt-4.1-mini` | plan, CRAG grade, guardrail JSON, feature extraction, summaries, injection classification | The majority of calls by volume — near-mechanical classification over short inputs. |
| **embeddings** | `azure/genailab-maas-text-embedding-3-large` (3072-dim) | all indexing and retrieval | **Never tiered.** Two embedding models in one collection either corrupt similarity silently or fail on dimension mismatch. |
| **vision** | `azure_ai/genailab-maas-Llama-3.2-90B-Vision-Instruct` | scanned pages, screenshots | Keeps image-only evidence searchable instead of indexing empty chunks |
| **speech** | `azure/genailab-maas-whisper` | voice fallback | Browser Speech API is primary |
| **local fallback** | `llama-3.2-3b-it` via Ollama | all chat tiers | Automatic when the hosted probe fails |

### 10.2 Determinism and gateway behaviour

- `LLM_TEMPERATURE = 0.1`; `chat_json()` forces `temperature=0` — triage must be
  reproducible.
- `_effective_temperature()` overrides to `1.0` for `gpt-5*`/`o1`/`o3` families,
  which **reject `temperature=0` outright** on this gateway. Without the clamp,
  every deep-tier call failed mid-triage with `UnsupportedParamsError`.
- Timeout 60s per call, one retry, all calls wrapped in `with_timeout()`.
- `@lru_cache` on client, model handle and embedding handle construction. No
  response caching — a cached triage decision would hide model drift.

### 10.3 Provider resolution and fallback

`resolve_provider()` probes the configured fast model once at boot with a real
`ping` (10s invoke, 12s wall) and caches the outcome for the process lifetime. On
failure every chat tier collapses to local Ollama.

**Embeddings deliberately do not follow that split.** They fall back to local
`gte-large` only when the hosted embedding call itself raises, and log loudly on
every occurrence, because anything embedded in that window sits in a different
vector space and requires a reseed once hosted service recovers. This is a stated
trade-off — dead-lettering every ticket for the duration of an outage was judged
worse — not a silent one.

### 10.4 Avoiding lock-in

| Swappable | How |
|---|---|
| Chat provider | `LLM_BASE_URL` / `LLM_API_KEY`, independent of the embedding endpoint precisely so a chat-only provider (e.g. DeepSeek) does not break retrieval |
| Model per tier | `LLM_MODEL`, `FAST_LLM_MODEL`, `REASONING_MODEL` |
| Embedding model | `EMBEDDING_MODEL` — **requires a reseed**, and the config says so |
| Vector store | One module, `db/vectordb/vector_store.py` |
| Ticketing system | One class implementing `TicketSource` |
| Retrieval strategy | `RETRIEVAL_MODE`, `RERANK_ENABLED` |

