## 13. Security, identity and access governance

| Concern | Implementation | Prototype gap |
|---|---|---|
| Authentication | JWT, HS256, 12h expiry; Werkzeug salted password hashes | No SSO/OIDC; no refresh tokens |
| Authorisation | Role (`admin`/`manager`/`engineer`/`viewer`) + team clearances in the token | — |
| Data access | ACL inside the Chroma `where` clause and inside the SQL query (`_scope_ticket_query`) | — |
| Rate limiting | Per-route, per-minute; login 10/min, sync 6/min, recalculation 4/min | In-process only; needs shared state behind multiple workers |
| Secrets | `.env`, git-ignored; empty defaults mean "do not write" rather than a wrong guess | No vault integration |
| Transport | `DISABLE_SSL_VERIFY` defaults **true** for corporate TLS-inspecting proxies and local Ollama | **Must be `false` in production** |
| Audit | Hash-chained append-only log; `GET /api/audit/verify` names the first broken row | Same-database chain; a production deployment should ship it to append-only external storage |
| Webhook | `POST /api/integrations/webhook` is unauthenticated by design | **Requires a shared-secret header before facing a real network** |
| Misuse monitoring | Every block, denial and guardrail firing is audited and queryable | No alerting on anomaly rates |

**Least privilege by role:**

| Capability | viewer | engineer | manager | admin |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| See own team's queue and history | — | ✓ | ✓ (all teams) | ✓ |
| Ask the KB assistant | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ |
| Approve / override a decision | — | — | ✓ | ✓ |
| Trigger a Jira sync | — | — | ✓ | ✓ |
| Upload knowledge-base documents | — | — | ✓ | ✓ |
| Delete a document | — | — | — | ✓ |
| Bulk approve | — | — | — | ✓ |
| Read the audit log | — | — | — | ✓ |

> **Seeded-account caveat.** The demo account named `manager` carries the **`admin`**
> role (`db/sqlite/models.py::_DEMO_USERS`). The `manager` role is fully wired into
> every route guard, but no seeded account uses it — so the running demo does not
> exercise the narrower privilege set. Add a genuine `manager`-role account before
