## 16. Observability and evaluation

### 16.1 Tracing

Every request runs inside a `Trace` context manager recording per-stage latency,
prompt/completion tokens and estimated cost from a per-model price table. The last
200 traces are held in an in-process ring buffer and exposed, expandable, on the
Usage dashboard. Durable per-request metrics live in `chat_messages` and
`triage_runs`.

### 16.2 Audit

Append-only, hash-chained: each entry hashes the previous one. Any edit breaks the
chain and `verify_chain()` names the first bad row. Recorded events include login,
retrieval, guardrail block, tool denial, triage decision, override, approval, sync,
document upload and deletion.

### 16.3 Evaluation suites

| Suite | Command | Measures |
|---|---|---|
| KB quality | `POST /api/evals/run` | groundedness, context precision, context recall, hallucination, over 12 questions including ≥2 that must be refused |
| Triage accuracy | `POST /api/evals/run-triage` | classification accuracy, routing precision, priority MAE, confusion matrix, per-team fairness, severity bias — over held-out labelled tickets |
| Retrieval A/B | `run_retrieval_ab()` | hybrid vs vector hit rate over 12 probes |

The KB eval runs through the **real** `handle_message()` path, guardrails included
— it measures the shipped system, not a bypass.

