## 20. Operations runbook

| Symptom | Diagnosis | Action |
|---|---|---|
| Sync pulls 0 tickets | Watermark past everything, or Jira auth failure | `select * from sync_state`; check logs for `Jira search failed`; verify credentials |
| Every ticket `status=failed` | Model gateway unreachable and no local fallback | `GET /api/health` → check `provider`; start Ollama or fix the gateway |
| Confidence uniformly low | Corpus not seeded, or ACL excluding everything | `GET /api/health` → `indexed_chunks`; re-run `seed_vector_db.py --reset` |
| Retrieval returns nothing relevant | Embedding model changed without a reseed | Reseed; check logs for local-embedding fallback warnings |
| `DRIFT` in the inspector | An index run failed halfway | Re-poll that ticket, or `seed_vector_db.py --reset` |
| Jira writes fail silently | Custom field IDs wrong, or workflow transition name absent | Check logs for `no Jira transition named`; confirm names in `STATUS_TO_TRANSITION_NAME` |
| Approvals rejected with 409 | Triage never completed for that ticket | Re-triage it; do not force-approve — the guard is correct |
| Override reverted after a sync | Should not happen | `ingest_and_triage()` skips severity/team when `overridden_by` is set; check that the override actually persisted |
| Deep-tier calls fail with `UnsupportedParamsError` | A new `gpt-5*`-class model not matched by `_effective_temperature()` | Extend the model-family match |
| Poll cycle hangs | Nested thread-pool exhaustion | Confirm ticket parallelism still uses the dedicated `_TICKET_POOL` |

**Standard inspection:**

```bash
python db/inspect_db.py                      # both stores + consistency check
python db/inspect_db.py --sql "select external_id, severity, assigned_team, status from tickets"
curl http://127.0.0.1:5000/api/health        # live provider/model/chunk count
```

