## 22. Glossary

| Term | Meaning |
|---|---|
| **ADF** | Atlassian Document Format — the JSON document structure Jira Cloud v3 uses for descriptions and comments instead of plain text |
| **ACL** | Access control list — here, the per-chunk `allowed_roles`/`acl_<role>` metadata enforced inside the retrieval query |
| **BM25** | A lexical ranking function — matches exact terms, which is why it finds error codes that dense embeddings blur |
| **Band margin** | How far a priority score sits from a band boundary (25/50/75). Near a boundary the priority is a coin flip |
| **CRAG** | Corrective RAG — grading retrieved chunks for relevance and re-retrieving or declaring "no precedent" instead of using a bad match |
| **Dead letter** | A ticket whose processing failed permanently, preserved with its error rather than dropped |
| **Evidence coverage** | Share of decision-critical evidence actually retrieved versus assumed |
| **Gate (confidence)** | One of three named 0–1 signals; confidence is their minimum |
| **Gate (node)** | The graph node that decides whether a human must review the decision |
| **Groundedness** | Share of an answer's claims supported by the retrieved context |
| **Held-out set** | Labelled tickets deliberately excluded from the index, used to measure accuracy honestly |
| **HNSW** | The graph index Chroma uses to make nearest-neighbour search fast |
| **Precedent agreement** | Share of retrieved precedent tickets that were given the same priority as this decision |
| **RRF** | Reciprocal Rank Fusion — merges two ranked lists with incomparable score scales using `1/(k+rank)` |
| **Trace** | A per-request record of stages, latency, tokens and cost |
| **Watermark** | The last-seen `updated` timestamp, persisted so polling resumes rather than restarting |
